</spec>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___00009XL00000">
<ptxt>Remove Rear Floor Mat Rear
</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the rear floor mat rear.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B167257" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1></s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0009" proc-id="RM0550J___00009XO00000">
<ptxt>Remove Deck Trim Service Hole Cover (Rear Side Installation Position)
</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the bolt and the trunk (luggage compartment) hold belt striker.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B168649" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Remove the LH side using the same procedure.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1></s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0011" proc-id="RM0550J___00009XP00000">
<ptxt>Remove Deck Trim Cover Rear
</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Disengage the 10 claws and remove the deck trim cover rear.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B152868" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1></s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0012" proc-id="RM0550J___00009W300000">
<ptxt>Adjust Back Door Panel Sub-assembly</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>To adjust the back door upper end vertically and the back door upper end laterally, loosen the bolts first.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B155577" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>19.5</t-value1>
<t-value2>198</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<atten3>
<ptxt>When adjusting, use a service bolt to adjust the fit.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>When adjusting the back door rear end laterally and the back door lock striker assembly, use a torx socket wrench T40 to loosen the striker installation bolts until the striker can be moved. Using a brass bar, lightly tap the striker to adjust it.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B155576" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>11.5</t-value1>
<t-value2>116</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___00009ZC00000">
<ptxt>Install Deck Trim Cover Rear
</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Engage the 10 claws to install the deck trim cover rear.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B152868" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>After installation, check that the back door weatherstrip is not caught in the deck trim cover rear.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1></s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0015" proc-id="RM0550J___00009ZD00000">
<ptxt>Install Deck Trim Service Hole Cover (Rear Side Installation Position)
</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Install the trunk (luggage compartment) hold belt striker with the bolt.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B168649" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Install the LH side using the same procedure.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1></s-1>
<s-1 id="RM0000029TM002X_02_0018" proc-id="RM0550J___00009ZG00000">
<ptxt>Install Rear Floor Mat Rear
</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Install the rear floor mat rear.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B167257" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1></s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>